#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# decimal_form

#% text
# `decimal_form(x)` shows the number `x` as a plain decimal, never in scientific notation; `decimal_form(x, n)` with `n` significant digits.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The argument is evaluated first; `decimal_form` stays around the value as a display wrapper. The wrapper stays around the value: it is a display directive and changes no computation.

#% item
# It reaches into lists and expressions: every machine real inside is shown in decimal form.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
decimal_form(1.5e-8)
#% output
#= decimal_form(1.5e-8)

#% cell
decimal_form(123456789.0)
#% output
#= decimal_form(123456789.0)

#% cell
decimal_form([0.5, 2.0e10])
#% output
#= decimal_form([0.5, 20000000000.0])

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `number_form`, `scientific_form`, `engineering_form`
